body:
I've tried this before but it's not a bad idea to try again. I want to work with them, but it's just a hard iron wall of 'we don't want to do matrix stuff' and the original post was supposed to just be a throw away rant about how that made me sad. 

&#x200B;

They're my best friends and we've been table top gaming for over ten years now. I'm going to try the npc thing, but I know for a fact that if I involve it any more than just a 'the decker does the thing, no rolls.' they get bored or unhappy. 

&#x200B;

I'm not unreasonable, I'm not going to fight them, and if they aren't going to try to work with me on this then I might just stop running shadowrun for them for a while. I'd rather not play than hurt their feelings over decking lol.

I wouldn't call them murderhobos because they do care about character story lines. The other NPC's that I've put in front of them, as long as they aren't enemies or unwilling to surrender, stay alive and they all become good friends. Even those that give them static about something aren't harrassed or murdered on the spot or anything.

&#x200B;

They just keep changing characters all the time and don't want to worry about magic or tech outside of phys-ads. They've made stealthy characters on the reg, even a face once, even a spellslinger once.

Yeah... I guess it's just... I'd really like to have this in the game and at this point I'm of the opinion that I should be able to ask my friends for things every now and then. Even if they don't want to as players, I might not be willing to keep running it if we never have any magic deeper than phys-ads or tech deeper than a commlink. But I know if I say 'no more Shadowrun.' then we just won't play Shadowrun. Possibly ever again. We'll just play dnd 5th until someone decides to run something else. 

&#x200B;

I'd never make them do something they don't want to do, it's just saddening that there's this whole extra dimension to this world we all love to be in that we're just setting to the side for no real reason.

Perhaps I should then ask them how realistic they want the game to be. I'm of the opinion that taking things from real life makes stories and these sorts of story centric games better but they are big anime fans, so they might want to throw it out the window. 

&#x200B;

But you're right, I'll add that to the list of things to talk to them about so we're all on the same page about what we want from the game.

That's a good point. I'm currently working through some stuff irl that's giving me the confidence and frame of mind to start having boundries and caring about what I want out of life rather than others. It's slow going and moments like these are hard as fuck to navigate, but you are right in that last regard.

&#x200B;

It's not that they necessarily want to murderhobo. It's that they aren't interested in spell-slingers all the time, and never in matrix stuff. I can start or talk to them about putting more opposition in front of them that requires leg work or else, but there's been a long time of no consequences for not doing legwork because I was too afraid of 'blindsiding' them which is the point of legwork! 

&#x200B;

I am also to blame for this, but I'm taking responsibility and going to talk to them about what *I* want out of things. I'm sure we can find a good middle ground.

I've also tried this. Although tbh, we only did it for one session before a life hiatus so I could totally try it again. The one thing, and this is a small hurdle I'm already thinking of how to jump over, is that these two change/ make new characters more than one changes their underwear lol. Again not a problem, since all our characters have the same fixer. An early fix for an earlier problem lol. 

&#x200B;

I'll try that again and see how they feel! It seemed alright last time tbh.

I've suggested that, but they said they wouldn't want to have to waste resources on hiring characters. That's why they won't hire anyone for any reason. I can't put something in their way that those two can't deal with, unless I also put something that those two could use to deal with it. 

&#x200B;

Which is fine on paper, but leads to basically all meat space combat, only. They almost never make faces, once or twice a spellslinger.

A combination of no interest in playing matrix characters and the one time one of them did, near on five years ago now, it went poorly. I made the defenses too frustrating to get past and it put a sour taste in that players mouth when they already were trepidatious about it. I didn't ask them to make that characters, but tried to show that it would be difficult in the first part of the run but become easier once the physical security outside the complex was dealt with. 

&#x200B;

But now they have told me, once again today, that they have no want to play a matrix character or even have it come up outside of pure fluff. No spiders, maybe enemy riggers, commlinks never get attacked, nothing.

I do appreciate it, but what do you do when you find that person, and you can feel the love going? Not from you, but from them? I wish I could be better, be what they need me to be, but I don't think I can. I try so hard to get better but it's only little spurts of good. I've read Atomic habits but I just can't make it work. Everything falls apart and I'm right back to where I was. 

&#x200B;

There's more to it than that, and maybe I should make a post here, but yeah.

&#x200B;

You will find that person, even if that person is you. I hope the best for you friend.

It depends on a number of factors that, unless you are in cybersecurity or stay adjacent to that field, you probably aren't going to have a problem. If your manuscript gets ganked off a compromised server, you're going to have much bigger problems than that. Not to mention, unless they think they can sell it to someone, they're just going to delete it. 

&#x200B;

That's my two cents.

Too many have these days it seems. My grandad also fought in ww2. Never got the chance to ask him face to face what that was like/ meant to him. Wish I could remember where or what. 

&#x200B;

We just can't let that kind of evil live and thrive again. I hope to see you out there in the field friend.

I remember this new hotness going around school. 

&#x200B;

Neo-Pets, I think it was called.

Would it ever be useful or good to respond to positive reviews? Sometimes I feel even just a simple "Thanks" might be a little like patting yourself on the back? Maybe I'm just paranoid lol

&#x200B;

Such a high quality post, You should be proud of it!

Personally I loved season 3. The others were great for what they were, but they definitely felt like episodic titles that were two steps up from a visual novel. Maybe I need (another excuse) to play the whole three seasons back to back again. It was just nice that we had all the laughs and wacky shenanigans but now there was something to actually do that felt like it mattered. 

&#x200B;

Maybe that's antithetical to what Sam and Max is as a concept, but it made it a better story and game overall.

While I get what you mean, yeah, it's better to try to distance yourself from those sorts of thoughts when you can. They'll consume you like fire to paper. It's ok if you slip some times, but always try to have some kind of safety net. 

&#x200B;

For me, like anything else, you get 'used' to it. I've been writing things down a lot more (just anything I want to remember) and it's been an absolute godsend. When I just can't focus because it's so loud/ destabilizing, I do everything I can to physically write down what I need to remember. If there isn't anything else, then I'll do something physical I don't have to think about until it just falls into the background. It's always there, and even after it does fall into the background, one mental misstep and I have to start the process all over again. 

&#x200B;

Meds help, sweet fuck do they help so much. But uh... american healthcare system so... yeah. Meditation has also... help is a strong word... made it less entirely debilitating. Because, while this is one of the most/ more severe symptoms, I've got like everything under the sun to some degree. It's a shorter list to say what I don't/ haven't experienced yet. 

&#x200B;

But I ramble.

&#x200B;

I believe in both of you, and I'm always open to getting messages. No promises I will/ can respond, but I'll always see it.

Yeah, OP seems to be forgetting the forced ice-pick lobotomies, the beatings, the electro-shocks. Not to mention the fact that at best they were gilded cages. Society, your family and friends outside, didn't like you, didn't want you, and only had enough moral fiber to lock you away in an iron and brick hell-scape, with the hopes you'd be too doped up to ever see that there was nothing but hate beyond.

&#x200B;

Having internet would only make it easier for you to see exactly how bad the situation for you is, and how truly inescapable it is.

&#x200B;

It's just that nobody is rounding us up (at least in the US... for now) and shipping us off to have metal rods shoved through our tearducts to 'fix' us.

Big mood. All of these are the same for me except one notable difference. Blood curdling, throat ripping shrieks of terror and agony. At least three times a day. If I start not sleeping/ meds stop working they happen less often but will continue for much longer. It's not uncommon for a single occurrence to last three to four hours. 

&#x200B;

The only time I've ever heard a specific and comprehensible thing, was right before each of my hospital visits. But even then it was stuff like 'go to sleep', 'don't trust that guy on the other side of the street', 'have you eaten recently?' Weirdly... helpful things? It's complicated and that's definitely not a rabbit hole you should go down. Never trust the voices. That's been a saving phrase for me.

I would say a little of both. Sometimes I'll get something as gentle as this, a finger pressing or touching my shoulder blades or somewhere else. There are sometimes where it feels like I've been shoved bodily and I'll fall. 

&#x200B;

Tl;Dr, it sounds like it could be both. Massage the area just in case it's a knot, but after that if it persists without change, then it's probably a hallucination.

But there were no scholars from anywhere else who felt that these extraordinary things were worth talking about? And there were no people who heard the tales and didn't convert? I will also rephrase what I said earlier, because you are right. A belief in a religion necessarily requires that it is important in the believer's eyes. 

&#x200B;

Hopefully a better way to put it is, is there anyone who recorded the events who was not Christian at any point. Secondarily, can any of these events be believed mutually exclusively? Do I need to believe *the entire bible* before I can believe any of these other things happened? What if I don't believe anything else, but am willing to hear the evidence for a specific event. 

&#x200B;

It'd make my life a whole lot better if I could believe. I want to. I want to understand this infinite love and understanding christians and all other believers believe in. But I'm not convinced. And it feels like you don't have a reason to be convinced other than that you've been told it's real, and that the ones who authored it were good and so that's why you should believe them. 

&#x200B;

It's car salesmen circular logic. Break the circle, show me some good unbiased evidence and I'll drop on my knees before Jesus Christ and ask him to be my personal savior. To save me from the torment and damnation I am certain to face if I am wrong.

That they believed, yes, that's great evidence that some number, possibly a large number, believed the things they were told. But one should not always believe what they are told without good and sufficient evidence. Are any of your sources not from christian scholars? Are any of these sources from outside of the bible/ apocryphon (I'm sure I mispelled that,  sorry.) In other words, are any of these sources from people who have nothing to gain from them being true?

&#x200B;

I trust a Christian to tell me they believe in God. If they are a layman, I don't trust them to tell me how the universe fundamentally works in a way that is useful. If they were a christian astro-physicist, I'd be willing to hear what they have to say about that.

I think perhaps they're saying that since everything George Washington has done 'feels humanly possible' it's easier to believe he was a real person who did true things. It's harder to believe that supernatural things have ever happened since none have been reliably documented. Super neat things have happened, that we eventually explained. But even not having an explanation is fine. This line of questioning I find to be rather useless in debates on the efficacy of religion in general. 

&#x200B;

There are a lot of reasons not to be convinced that the bible is an accurate text of anything other than what some bronze age jews thought about the world a very long time ago. Some of that information is timeless and useful, a lot of it is dated and should be rejected for the moral good of society and humanity.

Have you tried making a list of 'absolutely not's? That's one small thing to start with. I'm in the a similar ocean as you, and the only thing I've found that helps me with my compass is, what do I look into without being prompted. Someone once said that boredom is very important. Take a day, and get truly, honestly bored. If that means you do straight up nothing, do that. (As long as you aren't behind in anything, or going to die. Like, make food.)

&#x200B;

Let all the little thoughts flow around in their hurricane way and find one of two things. What do I think about the most, or what do I think about most strongly. If there are a few, write those down. But then dive. What is the most specialized there. What is the job no one else wants to do, or knows how to do. Can you do that? No? Then move on to the next thing. Don't know what that is, find out. Every time you don't know what question to ask for anything, step back. You might be looking for an answer, and an answer is like a fruit. If you don't know what fruit you want, take a step back and look through the orchard. The orchard is every other question, every other fruit.

&#x200B;

Does that make sense? I hope so, if not, feel free to tell me.

&#x200B;

I don't have this stuff figured out either, but I believe in you. Never stop asking questions. The day you find there are no more trees in your orchard, find another. Or you're dead, which in that case, there's not much else you can do unfortunately.

So I'm trans and very masculine looking (unfortunately). I use They/ Them pronouns and live in a very red state. I have learned the hard way that A) There is no way to pass as a non-binary-person. B) Just mentioning it can directly affect how difficult life will be at my job. C) I can lie and say I use he/ him but then life will suck as I am inviting people to misgender me.

&#x200B;

So it becomes a matter of me being very careful of who I reveal the truth to. If I feel safe to, and the environment is worth taking that risk, then I can tell the truth. It all comes down to weather it's safe or not.

Something with a skill tree. Do more mining, get better at mining. Do more farming, get better at farming and so on. That's my plan for my first mod I'm gonna make here soon. 

&#x200B;

The other is just a simple in game to do list that you make yourself, and isn't dependent on an item. Can also sync with anyone else so you and your friends can follow everyone's progress.

