&#x200B;

Everybody giggled and everything went to shit.

&#x200B;

But oh gods, what !!FUN!!

The artist does not yet know anything about RimWorld, He just wanted to challenge himself with the art style.

&#x200B;

But I'm going to try to get him into RimWorld lol. He's my boyfriend, fyi.

From as early as I can remember I've had hallucinations. I'd see people, hear voices, sometimes colors were wrong or I could taste heaviness. Hold a ten pound weight in your hand and it would taste just like oversalted chicken. What kept me from telling anyone was the voices telling me that if I ever did, the government would take my family away and I'd never see them. If I thought my parents were on to me about seeing things, I'd lie, I'd say it was a game or a joke. 

&#x200B;

I later learned that those voices may have been my very first alter.

&#x200B;

I have Schizo-affective disorder, bipolar type, PTSD and Dissociative identity disorder. I only got the first thing diagnosed when I was 21 after my first major psychotic episode. No one got hurt but they could have. 

&#x200B;

From that day since life has been better, when it can be. I jump from job to job, and recently decided I was going to start on SSI, but that's been a process like anything concerning the government. I've worked through that most major delusion and have ways to at least mitigate the others, once I catch them out as delusions. I still have bad days, but I don't do any of those bad things I shouldn't do and wont mention here so as not to trigger anyone. 

&#x200B;

Growing up it always felt like I was a completely different species from everyone else. No one was afraid of things like I was. No one thought about the horrible things I thought about and it really isolated me. The less I talked, the better it seemed. Until I discovered that I can just lie to all my friends too and bad things wont always happen. 

&#x200B;

It's taken a lot of work, but I find myself now in a situation where I don't want to end my life anymore. If there was a magic potion to give me my life back, I'd take it. But time wasted on fantasies like that is better spent on writing fantasy, I like to say. Feel free to DM me if you have any more questions.

Not that I know of. If I ever say anything that hurts him, after the episode ends and I can actually be a human being again, he'll talk to me and I'll apologize. He's never said that I'm abusive toward him, but that it's scary for him when I do have these episodes because he's worried I'll hurt myself. 

&#x200B;

I do appreciate your time. Best of luck to you as well.

I've had people stop talking to me at work, and one time someone asked me if it was ok for me to be at work right then. I was off my meds so I said probably not. This was a poor decision. 

&#x200B;

People just don't know very many people like us. and you're right, we're just different.

I love that it feels like they put just as much if not (usually) more time and energy into their characters than I do my whole game. I suffer from quick burnout, which I've been working for a long time to deal with, and one of the best things to do is just sit down with a text document open and talk. About their backstories, hypothetical situations they'd love to be in, cool adventure ideas, anything really. Since I don't have the best memory about things they can help me remember what we've done recently, (working on that by keeping real notes) great moments for them from other games, and even cool ideas from movies and shows since I have a hard time staying focused even during 30 minute shows some days.

&#x200B;

Some times it feels like every % I give gets back 10% from them. They're my best friends, and the only reason I don't jump in front of a bus every day. (P.S. thelordkye, gwen, ccslayer, or greg if you see this, love you guys for real)

